    {
      "title": "From Rerum Novarum to Magnifica Humanitas: What Does It Mean for AI to Benefit Humanity?",
      "start": "2026-12-04T15:45:00.586000Z",
      "end": "2026-12-04T17:00:00.586000Z",
      "venue": "Notre Dame campus",
      "locality": "Notre Dame campus, Notre Dame campus, Notre Dame, Indiana, United States",
      "description": "About the Talk:Join us on Notre Dame campus for this Forum talk!From the Industrial Revolution to the rise of artificial intelligence, technological change has raised enduring questions about human dignity, opportunity, and responsibility. Bringing together perspectives from OpenAI and Catholic thinkers, this conversation will explore what earlier periods of transformation can teach us about the choices we face today. Drawing on Rerum Novarum and Magnifica Humanitas, panelists will consider AI's potential to improve people's lives, the risks and limits that deserve attention, and what it would take to ensure its benefits are broadly shared.About the Speakers:James Hairston, Global Head of Innovation Policy, OpenAIJames Hairston leads global innovation policy at OpenAI, with responsibility for health, devices, and robotics. Before joining OpenAI, he spent a decade leading policy for virtual and augmented reality",
      "organizer": "OpenAI Forum",
      "sourceName": "forum.openai.com",
